0 L 2611 2029 Q 2611 2470 2422 2694 Q 2234 2918 1862 2918 Q 1658 2918 1472 2851 Q 1286 2784 1171 2643 Q 1056 2502 1056 2291 L 1056 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-71\" d=\"M 1613 1997 Q 1613 1376 1456 819 Q 1299 262 1036 -173 Q 774 -608 454 -877 L -32 -877 Q 314 -570 576 -134 Q 838 301 985 784 Q 1133 1267 1133 1715 L 1133 2266 Q 1133 2714 989 3194 Q 845 3674 585 4109 Q 326 4544 -32 4864 L 454 4864 Q 781 4589 1043 4150 Q 1306 3712 1459 3165 Q 1613 2618 1613 1997 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-20\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1\" transform=\"translate(62.09375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-13\" transform=\"translate(115.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1\" transform=\"translate(173.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-4\" transform=\"translate(226.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-c\" transform=\"translate(277.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-17\" transform=\"translate(302.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1c\" transform=\"translate(337.296875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e9\" transform=\"translate(387.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-70\" transform=\"translate(410.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" transform=\"translate(444.296875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e9\" transform=\"translate(504.296875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-17\" transform=\"translate(527.890625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-6\" transform=\"translate(562.578125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-4\" transform=\"translate(617.484375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-b\" transform=\"translate(667.78125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-11\" transform=\"translate(724.578125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-c\" transform=\"translate(781.375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-4\" transform=\"translate(806.375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-c\" transform=\"translate(856.671875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1\" transform=\"translate(881.671875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-11\" transform=\"translate(935.078125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-16\" transform=\"translate(991.875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-71\" transform=\"translate(1040.578125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p7bf8f1631e\"><rect x=\"40.7\" y=\"28\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"133.056\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Expected demand vs capacity","note":null},"answer":"<p>Repairs: 150 days × 55 + 150 days × 25 = <b>12,000</b>.</p> <p>Revenue: 12,000 × $28 = $336k. Contribution after parts (70%): $235k.</p> <p>Profit: $235k − $171k = <b>$64k a year</b>. Payback: $150k ÷ $64k = <b>2.3 years</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> it meets the three-year hurdle, but only just.</p>","note":"Fixed costs per year: rent $36k, technicians $120k, other $15k."},{"q":"In winter, how much technician time is idle? The owners are considering a student plan: $9 a month for two services a year. They expect 800 sign-ups, and each service uses about $6 of parts. What is it worth?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Winter idle capacity: 1 − 25 ÷ 60 = <b>58%</b>.</p> <p>Plan revenue: 800 × $9 × 12 = $86.4k. Services: 1,600 at about $6 of parts each = −$9.6k (labour is free: it uses idle winter time).</p> <p>Cannibalisation: if 40% of subscribers would have paid for about 1.5 repairs a year anyway: −$9.4k of lost margin.</p> <p>Net: <b>+$67.4k a year</b>, which would cut payback to about 1.1 years.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> worth it, as long as services are booked into winter. Let subscribers book only from October to March.</p>"},{"q":"What else could fill winter capacity?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Fleet contracts</b>: maintain bikes for delivery companies, hotels and bike-share operators</li> <li><b>Winter service</b> promotion: lights, brakes and tyres before the dark months</li> <li><b>Refurbish and sell used bikes</b> to students in September</li> <li><b>Flex staff</b>: a seasonal technician in summer instead of a third full-time one</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Open the Utrecht shop: it should make about $64k a year and pay back in 2.3 years, inside the three-year hurdle. Its weakness is winter, when 58% of technician time is idle. A student plan that books services into October to March adds about $67.4k a year and cuts payback to 1.1 years; fleet contracts could add more. Risk: a weak first summer while the shop builds awareness. Next step: talk to two local fleet operators before signing the lease.","great":["Builds revenue by season, not with one average","Measures idle capacity","Counts cannibalisation in the subscription maths","Uses idle time as a near-free resource"],"id":32,"slug":"spoke-sprocket"}